@@ -81,6 +81,11 @@ An ordered unique key that a public unique selector can use to name one record.
 A model can have several addressable keys.
 _Avoid_: Identity fields, unique field set
 
+**Compound selector**:
+The model-local public query name for a compound ID or compound unique tuple.
+It names the tuple in unique selectors and is not a model field.
+_Avoid_: Compound field
+
 **Reference key**:
 The ordered target fields to which a relation points. A reference key can differ
 from the target's row key, such as when a relation references a compound unique
@@ -142,6 +147,28 @@ membership. Distinguishing delete-and-reinsert of the same key requires an
 explicit version fact.
 _Avoid_: Same ID, old ID/new ID
 
+**Record occurrence**:
+One position at which an operation selects, produces, or returns a record.
+Equal row keys alone do not make two occurrences interchangeable.
+_Avoid_: Record identity when the position or its observation matters
+
+**Record selection**:
+The instructions that identify the record an occurrence may consume, through a
+query or an exact earlier record output. Selection is not proof of existence.
+_Avoid_: Captured record when only the selection instructions are known
+
+**Record observation**:
+What a selection observed at a particular execution point: an absent target or
+one exact captured record. An earlier absence does not settle every later use
+of the same selection.
+_Avoid_: Selection, reusable absence
+
+**Retained requirement**:
+A captured identity, membership or condition that must remain true when later
+work consumes it. The initial observation and its continuing requirement are
+different facts.
+_Avoid_: Input validation, selection filter when continuing truth is meant
+
